.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: MIT
.Dd October 12, 2026
.Dt DTFL_SET_LOG_HOOK 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm dtfl_set_log_hook
.Nd install the libdtfl diagnostic log hook
.Sh LIBRARY
Timely and differential dataflow library
.Pq libdtfl , \-ldtfl
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In dtfl/base.h
.Ft void
.Fn dtfl_set_log_hook "dtfl_log_fn fn" "void *ctx"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
libdtfl emits human-readable diagnostics, such as a failure to start a
worker thread, through a log hook.
.Fn dtfl_set_log_hook
installs
.Fa fn ,
which is called with a level, a message, and the
.Fa ctx
passed here:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
typedef enum dtfl_log_level {
	DTFL_LOG_DEBUG, DTFL_LOG_INFO, DTFL_LOG_WARN, DTFL_LOG_ERROR
} dtfl_log_level;
typedef void (*dtfl_log_fn)(dtfl_log_level level, const char *msg,
    void *ctx);
.Ed
.Pp
With no hook installed, libdtfl writes
.Dv DTFL_LOG_WARN
and
.Dv DTFL_LOG_ERROR
messages to standard error and drops
.Dv DTFL_LOG_DEBUG
and
.Dv DTFL_LOG_INFO ,
so the library is quiet by default.
Passing
.Dv NULL
for
.Fa fn
restores that default.
.Pp
This diagnostic log is separate from the structured timely and
differential event logging reached through
.In dtfl/log.h ,
which carries machine-readable events and is not affected by this
hook.
.Pp
The hook is process-wide and must be installed before the first
.Fn dtfl_execute ,
like the allocation, panic and thread hooks; see
.Xr dtfl_embedding 7 .
.Sh EXAMPLES
A PostgreSQL extension maps the levels to
.Fn elog ,
but not
.Dv DTFL_LOG_ERROR
to
.Dv ERROR :
the hook runs inside libdtfl, and an error that longjmps out leaves the
worker unusable
.Pq Xr dtfl_embedding 7 :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
static void
pg_log(dtfl_log_level level, const char *msg, void *ctx)
{
	int elevel[] = { DEBUG1, LOG, WARNING, LOG };
	elog(elevel[level], "dtfl: %s", msg);
}

dtfl_set_log_hook(pg_log, NULL);
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr dtfl_set_alloc_hooks 3 ,
.Xr dtfl_set_thread_hooks 3 ,
.Xr dtfl 7 ,
.Xr dtfl_embedding 7
.Sh HISTORY
Rust libraries log through the
.Ql log
or
.Ql tracing
facade; this hook is the C equivalent, letting an embedding host route
diagnostics into its own logging.
.Sh THREAD SAFETY
.Fn dtfl_set_log_hook
must be called before the first
.Fn dtfl_execute .
Once installed, the hook may be called from any worker thread, so it
must be reentrant and thread-safe.
